2026-10-23T11:19:23.7547363Z cargo deny check
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1350000Z error[vulnerability]: Non-constant-time mask generation and `u128` comparisons
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1356464Z    ┌─ /home/runner/work/_temp/nsealr-product/nsealr/Cargo.lock:11:1
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1359315Z    │
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1366864Z 11 │ ctutils 0.4.3 registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1368642Z    │ ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ security vulnerability detected
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1369739Z    │
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1370436Z    ├ ID: RUSTSEC-2026-0385
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1371429Z    ├ Advisory: https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0385
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1372404Z    ├ ## Summary
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1372996Z      
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1373835Z      The `ctutils::Choice` type has mask generation functions for each unsigned
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1375107Z      integer size (`u8`, `u16`, `u32`, `u64`, `u128`). These are `const fn` and
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1376540Z      therefore can't reuse the `asm!`-backed mask generation in the `cmov` crate
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1377716Z      that's otherwise used to ensure constant-time.
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1378516Z      
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1379347Z      In releases prior to v0.4.4, the generated code from these functions could
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1380630Z      include a branch on commonly used platforms. This has been corrected in this
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1381850Z      release and now verified on several platforms using BINSEC.
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1382701Z      
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1383585Z      Additionally, `u128` comparison operations provided via `ctutils::Choice` and
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1384950Z      intended to work in constant-time were generating branches on 32-bit targets.
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1386448Z      This has been resolved via a special case implementation of these functions
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1387376Z      for such targets.
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1387895Z      
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1388348Z      ## Impact
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1388835Z      
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1389532Z      Branch instructions on secret values can potentially leak such values via
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1390631Z      covert channels. This can enable attackers to potentially recover such secrets.
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1391506Z      
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1391991Z      ## Resolution
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1392508Z      
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1395775Z      This has been resolved by calling `Choice::to_u8()` when generating the mask,
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1397223Z      which in turn uses `black_box` as an optimization barrier. Verification that
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1398316Z      this resulted in the desired change in the generated assembly across a variety
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1399437Z      of target CPU architectures was performed by BINSEC, which now runs
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1400301Z      automatically in CI using `cargo checkct`.
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1401300Z    ├ Announcement: https://github.com/RustCrypto/utils/pull/1569
2026-10-23T11:19:24.1402327Z    ├ Solution: Upgrade to >=0.4.4 (try `cargo update -p ctutils`)
